      "content": "look i'm really not interested in the goblin stuff, i just need to fix the production line. can we stick to the technical stuff? \n\nyou mentioned heat and ink compatibility. if the temperature is high enough and the ink is the right type, could it be the fabric's chemical structure? like, maybe some parts of the polyester fibers are resisting the dye or absorbing it differently? how would that work chemically?",
